      "message": "@bobbycasey@google.com\n\n`set_rtc_alarm`, `get_rtc_diff`, and `reset_rtc_alarm` are defined in `clock-f.c`, which is only included for the `bloonchipper` build. They are not included for `dartmonkey`.\n\nFor `helipilot`, there are additional issues:\n\nThe `rtc_time_reg` struct is defined `clock_chip`. However, this might be a different header with different relative path for `npcx`\n```\ntest/stm32f_rtc.c:12:15: note: forward declaration of \u0027struct rtc_time_reg\u0027\n   12 | static struct rtc_time_reg rtc_irq;\n```\n\nThe below error can be resolved for `helipilot` by including `timer.h`. I am not sure if there is some circular inclusion for `bloonchipper`\n```\ntest/stm32f_rtc.c:19:33: error: use of undeclared identifier \u0027MSEC\u0027\n   19 | static const int delay_tol_us \u003d MSEC / 2;\n```\n\nthe below error can be resolved by including `atomic.h`. Not sure why this was not an issue for `bloonchipper` or `dartmonkey`\n```\ntest/stm32f_rtc.c:26:2: error: call to undeclared function \u0027atomic_add\u0027; ISO C99 and later do not support implicit function declarations [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]\n   26 |         atomic_add(\u0026rtc_fired, 1);\n```",
